  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "For the octahedral complex, which of the following <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>-electron configuration will give maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CFSE</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rhox4",
      "text": "high&nbsp;spin,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "35MDl",
      "text": "low spin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j7oHp",
      "text": "Iow spin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Sl5YM",
      "text": "high spin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>nt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>ne</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math>number of electrons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>nt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ne</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CFSE</mi></math> of given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math> -electrons configuration are as follows</p><p>a. For high spin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>CFSE</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>b. For low spin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math>;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>CFSE</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>c. For low spin&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>CFSE</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>d. For high spin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>CFSE</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Neglecting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>ve</mi></math> sign (as it indicates that energy is released).</p><p>Hence, maximum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>CFSE</mi></mfenced></math> value is shown by low spin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math> configuration.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
